# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization.
# `eol=lf` additionally FORCES line endings to LF in the repository
# regardless of the committer's local core.autocrlf setting (e.g. Git for
# Windows often defaults to converting LF -> CRLF on checkout/commit).
# Without this, a line-ending-only "change" can make git (and therefore
# SonarCloud's New Code detection) think an entire file was modified even
# when only a few real lines changed — inflating New Code duplication/
# issue counts with old, already-existing content that just got swept up
# by the line-ending churn.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Keep Windows-only script files as CRLF, since that's what they need.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
